WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.380
The advantage of a challenge is that
you're saying, okay, for the next

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.540
30 days or for the next 90 days, I'm
gonna push myself a little further.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.310
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:17.110
Uh, today I wanna talk about the next
series of challenges at LingQ, 90-Day

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.100
Challenges or 30 Day Challenges.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.250
Remember, if you enjoy these videos,
please subscribe, click on the bell for

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.360
notifications, and if you follow me on a
podcast service, please leave a comment.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:33.440
So, uh, I have been involved in a
number of language challenges at LingQ.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.410
Why do I do it and why do I think
it's a good idea for, for learners

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.480
to push themselves in this way?

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.790
Um, you know, one of the main issues,
in fact I've said before that the,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.840
the with language learning is a
function of, of attitude and of

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.030
time, time spent with a language.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.739
Uh, so attitude.

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:55.320
A large part of attitude is
of course our motivation.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.310
How keen we are.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.405
And in an ideal world, every day
we wake up and we just can't wait

00:01:00.405 --> 00:01:01.605
to start learning our language.

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:02.535
We can't wait to listen.

00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:07.035
We can't wait to read, and we're happy and
everything is, you know, on the up and up.

00:01:07.395 --> 00:01:09.975
Unfortunately, that's not always the case.

00:01:10.304 --> 00:01:14.115
There are days when we don't
feel like listening to our,

00:01:14.175 --> 00:01:15.465
whatever we're listening to.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:19.815
There are days when we're discouraged,
when we're busy, we invent all kinds of

00:01:19.815 --> 00:01:24.255
reasons why we needn't bother, and yet
we know that, you know, staying with it.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.305
This idea of continuity is so
important to language learning.

00:01:28.305 --> 00:01:33.015
Even a little bit every day is gonna keep
us moving in the direction of fluency

00:01:33.015 --> 00:01:35.295
or whatever, you know, our goal is.

00:01:35.805 --> 00:01:39.550
So that's one of the reasons why at
LingQ we have a number of sort of,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.380
call it tricks to keep people going.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.730
Uh, the statistics in
themselves are motivating.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.350
They're motivating to motivating to me.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.580
How many words have I read?

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.200
How many words have I saved?

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.240
In other words, how many
LingQs have I created?

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.770
How many hours have I listened?

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.600
When I look back in my profile page,
and I see when I started and when

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.320
I was active and how active I've
been over the last little period

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.360
all of this is motivating to me.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.890
So the statistics are in themselves
motivating, but the advantage of a

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:16.815
challenge is then you're saying, okay, for
the next 30 days or for the next 90 days,

00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:19.545
I'm gonna push myself a little further.

00:02:20.055 --> 00:02:24.645
And one of the things that I think the
LingQ team has done that's, that's really

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:30.795
good now is that whereas before you had to
have, you know, you had specific targets.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.715
Like you had to save so many words.

00:02:32.765 --> 00:02:36.285
In other words, create so many LingQs
uh, you had to read so many words,

00:02:36.285 --> 00:02:37.795
you had to listen so many hours.

00:02:38.095 --> 00:02:43.215
There are very specific, you know,
activity related, uh, targets.

00:02:43.725 --> 00:02:48.465
And that's a bit unfair because, you
know, as I often say, you wanna keep

00:02:48.465 --> 00:02:50.355
doing the things that you enjoy doing.

00:02:50.565 --> 00:02:53.595
So some days you're more
inclined to listen or maybe

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.095
you only have time to listen.

00:02:55.394 --> 00:02:57.825
Some other days you're
more inclined to read.

00:02:57.825 --> 00:03:00.195
Maybe you're reading material
that you've already gone through.

00:03:00.515 --> 00:03:03.060
Some other day, you're going
through new materials, so you're,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.640
you're creating new LingQs.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:09.095
And so by kind of
merging, funging, every...

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.760
every activity into the, the concept
of coins, as long as you maintain the

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.830
target you've set for coins, uh, which
you can do in a variety of different

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.200
ways, you are able to maintain a streak.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:26.520
So not only is the target important
and the idea that you're committed,

00:03:27.405 --> 00:03:32.625
30 or a 90 day, uh, challenge
important, but I found this desire

00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:35.235
to maintain my street kept me going.

00:03:35.895 --> 00:03:40.305
And so you wanna be careful that you
set a level in terms of the coins per

00:03:40.305 --> 00:03:47.055
day that is sufficiently challenging
without being too difficult, so

00:03:47.055 --> 00:03:50.325
that it's kind of, you're pushing
yourself, but it's not too easy.

00:03:50.695 --> 00:03:54.300
And if you're able to do that, then you
get a great sense of sense of satisfaction

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:59.760
because we know that the brain, if the
brain is confronted with a task that's

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.320
a little difficult and is able to do it,
there is a great sense of satisfaction.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:08.430
If the task is too easy, then there
is very little stimulus from that.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.900
If the task is so difficult that we
simply can't maintain that level of

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.700
activity, then it's discouraging.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:18.540
So it's important to choose a level
that that works for you, that pushes

00:04:18.545 --> 00:04:23.025
you without being too difficult and
occasionally I, what I do, if I fall

00:04:23.025 --> 00:04:28.724
behind and I lose my streak, then I'm
able to take the coins that I've earned

00:04:28.784 --> 00:04:30.825
and use them to repair my streak.

00:04:30.945 --> 00:04:34.784
So if I, if I have a streak of 30
days, and then for whatever reason

00:04:34.784 --> 00:04:39.315
now I wasn't able to do anything, the
next day I'm able to repair my streak

00:04:39.375 --> 00:04:41.835
so that I now have a 31, 32, 33.

00:04:41.835 --> 00:04:43.844
And just keep that streak going.

00:04:44.025 --> 00:04:48.599
So, you know, and some of us may
be into several languages, so

00:04:48.659 --> 00:04:52.900
that's a bit of a disadvantage that
you can't merge across languages.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:59.340
So the solution there is to set, not
to tough a target in each of two or

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.690
three languages so that you're able to
maintain your activity in those languages.

00:05:03.989 --> 00:05:10.315
And so, uh, let's say, Uh, gonna
have a tougher sort of goal in, say,

00:05:10.315 --> 00:05:15.895
in my case, Persian and a somewhat
lower goal in Arabic and Turkish.

00:05:16.135 --> 00:05:21.885
Then I don't have to spend a lot of
time on the minor languages to maintain

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:26.395
that lesser, you know, goal, maintain
my streak, but at least I'm staying

00:05:26.395 --> 00:05:30.744
in touch with those languages while I
focus more effort on my main language.

00:05:31.104 --> 00:05:35.820
So check the, uh, uh, challenges at LingQ.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.410
Commit yourself to a challenge.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.490
You'll be happy you did.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.719
And then you can follow how other
LingQ members are doing by going to

00:05:42.719 --> 00:05:47.010
the community page and seeing who,
you know, who has the longest streak,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:51.030
who has, uh, you know, created the
most LingQs and so forth and so on.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:55.200
So it's, it's a fun way to connect
with others, which also is important

00:05:55.205 --> 00:05:59.010
in language learning, because sometimes
we can feel that it's a bit of a lonely

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:04.470
activity, but once we realize we're part
of a larger community  that, uh, are

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:08.370
working on whatever language it might be,
the language you're learning or some other

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:13.110
language, you can see the sort of, uh,
level of activity in different languages.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.640
I find that quite motivating.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:20.280
So with that, I would encourage you
to get involved here in the new year

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:25.380
in, uh, some kind of a challenge,
30 or 90 days push yourself.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.850
Not so hard that you can't keep up,
but not so easy that you don't really

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.645
feel that you've achieved very much.

00:06:32.375 --> 00:06:38.355
So best of luck to you on your challenges
and uh, you'll see in these, uh,

00:06:38.355 --> 00:06:42.195
videos that I'll leave with you that
I have had challenges in a number of

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.535
languages and it has pushed me forward.

00:06:44.865 --> 00:06:46.065
So good luck to you.

00:06:46.335 --> 00:06:46.965
Bye for now.

